===Etymology===
Via other European languages, ultimately borrowed from {{bor|lv|ms|Jepang|Japan}}, itself a [[Appendix:Glossary#borrowing|borrowing]] from {{etyl|nan|lv}} {{m|nan|日本|tr=Ji̍t-pún}}, literally “sunrise” (the same meaning of {{cog|ja|日本|tr=Nip-pon}}), made, like most other country names, into a feminine 4th-declension noun.

